{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "one-machine",
  "title": "Everything on one machine",
  "summary": "Follow a young product from one server to a load-balanced cluster: saturation, the ceiling of a bigger machine, and the single point of failure.",
  "level": "beginner",
  "minutes": 5,
  "project": {
    "name": "Everything on one machine",
    "serverProfile": {
      "os": "linux",
      "cpuCores": 4,
      "cpuGhz": 3.0,
      "ramGb": 16.0,
      "disk": {
        "kind": "ssd",
        "iops": 20000
      },
      "network": {
        "bandwidthMbps": 1000.0,
        "latencyMs": 0.5
      },
      "virtualization": "vm",
      "fdLimit": 65536
    },
    "trafficProfile": {
      "concurrentUsers": 1000,
      "requestsPerSecond": 150.0,
      "readRatio": 0.8,
      "spike": {
        "kind": "none"
      }
    },
    "topology": {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "client",
          "kind": "client",
          "label": "Users",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 120
          },
          "template": null,
          "settings": {},
          "replicas": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "app",
          "kind": "appServer",
          "label": "Everything on one machine",
          "position": {
            "x": 280,
            "y": 120
          },
          "template": null,
          "settings": {},
          "replicas": 1
        }
      ],
      "edges": [
        {
          "id": "e-client-app",
          "source": "client",
          "target": "app"
        }
      ]
    },
    "chaos": {
      "faults": [],
      "policy": {
        "timeoutMs": 10000.0,
        "maxRetries": 0,
        "backoffMs": 100.0
      }
    },
    "slo": {
      "p95Ms": 200.0,
      "maxErrorRate": 0.01
    }
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Today: one server is plenty",
      "narration": [
        "All your users talk to a single server. At 150 requests per second it is busy about a third of the time, so requests are answered quickly.",
        "Watch the dashed column above the server: it is the machine's capacity. The coloured fill shows how much of it is in use."
      ],
      "highlight": ["app"],
      "changes": [],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 30.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": true
        },
        {
          "kind": "bottleneck",
          "node": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Traffic triples",
      "narration": [
        "The product takes off and traffic jumps to 450 requests per second. This server can only do about 400, so work arrives faster than it leaves.",
        "Requests queue up, latency climbs, and once the waiting room is full new requests are turned away."
      ],
      "highlight": ["app"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "apply",
          "change": {
            "kind": "trafficRate",
            "rps": 450.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 30.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "bottleneck",
          "node": "app"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p95AboveMs",
          "value": 200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Buy a bigger machine",
      "narration": [
        "The quickest fix is vertical scaling: move to a machine with four times the cores. The same traffic now barely registers.",
        "No design change, no new failure modes. This is why it is usually the first thing people try."
      ],
      "highlight": ["app"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "apply",
          "change": {
            "kind": "server",
            "field": "cpuCores",
            "value": 16.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 30.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": true
        },
        {
          "kind": "bottleneck",
          "node": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Growth never stops",
      "narration": [
        "Traffic keeps growing, now past 2,000 requests per second. This is the biggest machine we are willing to buy, and it has run out of room.",
        "There is always a ceiling on how big a single machine can be, and the price climbs faster than the capacity."
      ],
      "highlight": ["app"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "apply",
          "change": {
            "kind": "trafficRate",
            "rps": 2200.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 30.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "bottleneck",
          "node": "app"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "One machine is one point of failure",
      "narration": [
        "Back to a manageable 450 requests per second, but now the server crashes for fifteen seconds and then restarts.",
        "While it is down, every single request fails. Capacity was not the problem this time: having only one of everything was."
      ],
      "highlight": ["app"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "apply",
          "change": {
            "kind": "trafficRate",
            "rps": 450.0
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "addFault",
          "fault": {
            "id": "crash-a",
            "target": "app",
            "kind": {
              "kind": "crash"
            },
            "startS": 10.0,
            "durationS": 15.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 40.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "errorRateAbove",
          "value": 0.25
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scale out behind a load balancer",
      "narration": [
        "Instead of one large machine, use three ordinary ones and put a load balancer in front. Each carries a third of the traffic.",
        "The same crash now takes out a third of the capacity instead of all of it. This simple load balancer does not notice that a server is down, so a third of requests still land on it."
      ],
      "highlight": ["lb", "app", "app2", "app3"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "apply",
          "change": {
            "kind": "server",
            "field": "cpuCores",
            "value": 4.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 40.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "errorRateAbove",
          "value": 0.03
        },
        {
          "kind": "errorRateBelow",
          "value": 0.3
        }
      ],
      "topology": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "client",
            "kind": "client",
            "label": "Users",
            "position": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 190
            },
            "template": null,
            "settings": {},
            "replicas": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "lb",
            "kind": "loadBalancer",
            "label": "Load balancer",
            "position": {
              "x": 300,
              "y": 190
            },
            "template": null,
            "settings": {},
            "replicas": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "app",
            "kind": "appServer",
            "label": "Server A",
            "position": {
              "x": 620,
              "y": 10
            },
            "template": null,
            "settings": {},
            "replicas": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "app2",
            "kind": "appServer",
            "label": "Server B",
            "position": {
              "x": 620,
              "y": 190
            },
            "template": null,
            "settings": {},
            "replicas": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "app3",
            "kind": "appServer",
            "label": "Server C",
            "position": {
              "x": 620,
              "y": 370
            },
            "template": null,
            "settings": {},
            "replicas": 1
          }
        ],
        "edges": [
          {
            "id": "e-client-lb",
            "source": "client",
            "target": "lb"
          },
          {
            "id": "e-lb-app",
            "source": "lb",
            "target": "app"
          },
          {
            "id": "e-lb-app2",
            "source": "lb",
            "target": "app2"
          },
          {
            "id": "e-lb-app3",
            "source": "lb",
            "target": "app3"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Retries route around the failure",
      "narration": [
        "Teach clients to try again. A retry goes back through the load balancer, which usually picks a healthy server this time.",
        "Most failed requests now succeed on their second or third attempt, so users barely notice the crash. Redundancy plus retries is what makes the design resilient."
      ],
      "highlight": ["lb"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "setPolicy",
          "policy": {
            "timeoutMs": 10000.0,
            "maxRetries": 3,
            "backoffMs": 20.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 40.0,
        "speed": 5
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": true
        },
        {
          "kind": "errorRateBelow",
          "value": 0.02
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
